      "id": "lem-two-step-expansions",
      "label": "Lemma 7",
      "line": 105,
      "proofDependencies": [
        "prop-one-step"
      ],
      "section": "construction",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:two-step-expansions}\nLet $\\phi_j\\in\\R$ be the angle of the unit eigenvector $e_{2j}$ for\nthe smaller eigenvalue at iteration $2j$.  Choose this angle continuously along the\nsequence.  Let $G_j$ be the corresponding gradient component in\n\\eqref{eq:coordinate-representation}, and define\n$C_k=x_k-g_k$.\nOn the invariant center manifold,\n\\begin{align}\n\\frac{G_{j+1}}{G_j}\n&=1-\\frac{13}{2}\\epsilon_j^4+O(\\epsilon_j^6),\n\\label{eq:G-map}\\\\\n\\phi_{j+1}-\\phi_j\n&=-3\\epsilon_j^2+O(\\epsilon_j^4),\n\\label{eq:phi-map}\\\\\nC_{2j+2}-C_{2j}\n&=-\\frac{116}{5}G_j\\epsilon_j^6e_{2j}\n+O(G_j\\epsilon_j^7),\n\\label{eq:C-map}\\\\\n\\|C_{2j+1}-C_{2j}\\|&=O(G_j\\epsilon_j^3).\n\\label{eq:C-half}\n\\end{align}\nThe two consecutive increments in the polar angle of the gradient within\na cycle are respectively\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:half-angles}\n-2\\epsilon_j^2+o(\\epsilon_j^2),\n\\qquad -\\epsilon_j^2+o(\\epsilon_j^2).\n\\end{equation}\nHere $e_{2j}$ is the first column of $R_{2j}$, expressed in the original\ncoordinates.",
      "statementDependencies": [],
      "title": "Control amplitude, angle, and center drift",
      "type": "Lemma",
      "paperMapping": "All five components: the O(ε⁶) amplitude remainder, frame rotation, full- and half-cycle center drift, and both within-cycle gradient-angle remainders.",
      "texLabel": "lem:two-step-expansions",
      "relatedDeclarations": [
