      "file": "ReasLib/Optimization/DFP/TwoPhaseOrbit/ScalarAsymptotics.lean",
      "id": "lem-scalar-asymptotics",
      "label": "Lemma 8",
      "line": 20,
      "proofDependencies": [
        "lem-two-step-expansions",
        "prop-one-step"
      ],
      "section": "construction",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:scalar-asymptotics}\nThere are limits $G_\\infty>0$ and $C_\\infty\\in\\R^2$ such that\n\\begin{align}\n\\epsilon_j&\\sim\\left(\\frac92j\\right)^{-1/3},\n\\label{eq:epsilon-asymptotic}\\\\\nG_j-G_\\infty&\\sim\\frac{13}{3}G_\\infty\\epsilon_j,\n\\label{eq:G-tail}\\\\\n\\|C_{2j}-C_\\infty\\|&=O(\\epsilon_j^3),\n\\qquad\n\\|C_{2j+1}-C_\\infty\\|=O(\\epsilon_j^3).\n\\label{eq:C-tail}\n\\end{align}\nAlso, $\\phi_j\\to-\\infty$, and the accumulation set $\\Gamma$ of\n$\\{x_k\\}$ is the full circle\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:limit-circle}\n\\Gamma=\\{C_\\infty+G_\\infty v:\\|v\\|=1\\}.\n\\end{equation}",
      "statementDependencies": [],
      "title": "Positive limiting amplitude and a limiting circle",
      "type": "Lemma",
      "paperMapping": "The complete scalar asymptotics theorem, including negative-infinite winding and equality of the full endpoint cluster set with the limiting circle; the circle theorem is also linked separately.",
      "texLabel": "lem:scalar-asymptotics",
      "relatedDeclarations": [
