    {
      "declaration": "DFP.SecantIteration.planarDegeneration",
      "dependencies": [],
      "dependencyEvidence": "compiled",
      "file": "ReasLib/Optimization/DFP/SecantDegeneration.lean",
      "id": "lem-planar-degeneration",
      "label": "Lemma 11",
      "line": 726,
      "proofDependencies": [],
      "section": "convergence",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:planar-degeneration}\nLet $f\\in C^2(\\R^2)$ be $\\mu$-strongly convex, where $\\mu>0$.\nConsider an infinite sequence of nonstationary iterates with\n$g_k=\\nabla f(x_k)$, $s_k=-\\alpha_kH_kg_k$,\n$x_{k+1}=x_k+s_k$, and $y_k=g_{k+1}-g_k$, where $H_k\\succ0$,\n$\\alpha_k>0$, and every step satisfies \\eqref{eq:armijo} and\n\\eqref{eq:weak-curvature} for fixed $0<c_1<c_2<1$.\nSuppose $H_ky_{k-1}=s_{k-1}$ for $k\\ge1$. Put\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:planar-scalar-definition}\n\\ell_k=\\|s_k\\|,\\qquad\n\\kappa_k=\\frac{s_k^Ty_k}{\\ell_k^2},\\qquad\n\\lambda_k=\\kappa_{k-1}\\det H_k\\quad(k\\ge1).\n\\end{equation}\nIf $x_k$ does not converge to the unique minimizer $x_*$, then\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:planar-degeneration}\n0<\\lambda_k\\le C\\ell_{k-1}\\ell_k\\longrightarrow0\n\\end{equation}\nfor all sufficiently large $k$, with $C$ independent of $k$.\nMoreover, $\\{H_k\\}$ is bounded and $\\lambda_{\\min}(H_k)\\to0$.",
      "statementDependencies": [],
      "title": "Nonconvergence forces planar secant degeneration",
      "type": "Lemma",
      "paperMapping": "The general positive-definite secant theorem, without a DFP update assumption. Lean’s lam k is the paper’s λₖ₊₁; the bound, limit, matrix boundedness, and smallest-eigenvalue limit are all included.",
